==================================================
5. ADDING SUPPLIES
==================================================

Support these entry paths:

A. QUICK ADD
- Name required.
- Photo optional.
- Category optional.
- Storage location optional.
- Save immediately.
- Everything else can be completed later.

B. DETAILED ADD
- All shared and category-specific fields.

C. SCAN BARCODE
- Read UPC/EAN and other deliberately supported formats.
- Search the local collection first.
- If found, offer:
  - View existing item.
  - Add quantity to an appropriate existing batch.
  - Add a separate batch/piece.
  - Create a distinct record if the user confirms.
- If not found, optionally attempt online lookup when an approved provider has been configured.
- If lookup fails, preserve the barcode and open manual entry.
- Never block saving because lookup is unavailable.

D. DUPLICATE ITEM
- Copy relevant product attributes.
- Let the user change color, dimensions, quantity, batch, and location.
- Do not accidentally duplicate reservations, consumption history, or project allocations.

E. CAPTURE NOW, ORGANIZE LATER
- Allow a user to capture multiple photos into a draft inbox.
- Let the user explicitly decide which photos belong to each supply.
- Do not assume every photo is a separate item.
- Drafts may remain incomplete.
- Before moving a draft into the main inventory, require a name.

Optional completeness cues:
- Needs name.
- Needs category.
- Needs location.
- Organized.

These are helpful cues, not overdue tasks or failure states.

