Do not imply that every project on these sites is free, beginner-friendly, available without an account, or validated by Craft Stash.

Explain:
- External sites have their own terms and privacy policies.
- Some content may require an account or payment.
- Craft Stash is not affiliated with these services.
- Supplies and instructions must be checked on the original source.

Use text names and original app artwork.
Do not copy site logos, project thumbnails, or pattern content.

Each directory entry should have:
- Name.
- Base URL.
- Craft tags.
- Brief factual description.
- Optional verified search template.
- Optional account/payment note.
- Enabled/disabled status.

Let users:
- Add their own destinations.
- Edit or remove suggestions.
- Disable all bundled suggestions.
- Restore defaults intentionally.

Do not guess deep-link/search URL formats.
If a site’s search template is not verified:
- Copy the generated query.
- Open the site’s verified landing page.
- Explain that the user can paste the query.

Open links in the user’s external browser.
No embedded web scraping.
No login integrations.
No requirement to install Pinterest, Ravelry-related apps, or any other proprietary app.
Do not hardcode a preferred browser or search provider.

Before release, review whether recommending named proprietary services requires F-Droid anti-feature disclosure.
External-browser use is not proof of exemption.

Keep source-directory configuration separate from matching logic so that source suggestions can be adjusted without weakening offline functionality.

If a stricter F-Droid configuration is needed, document an honest alternative using generic editable search prompts and user-added destinations.
Do not silently remove requested suggestions or claim approval.

==================================================
16. OPTIONAL BARCODE PRODUCT LOOKUP
==================================================

Separate barcode decoding from network lookup.

Create a provider interface so no single catalog is structurally required.

Do not ship a functioning integration until:
- API documentation is verified.
- Terms permit the intended app use.
- Data/image storage rights are understood.
- Rate limits and credentials are handled appropriately.
- F-Droid service/anti-feature implications are documented.

A candidate provider may be evaluated, but no provider coverage should be assumed.

Required behavior:
- Lookup only after an explicit user action or clearly enabled setting.
- Explain which identifier is sent.
- Preserve manual entry.
- Show an editable result preview.
- Never overwrite user edits silently.
- Store provenance for imported fields where practical.
- Cache data only where terms permit.
- Download and retain images only where permitted.
- Do not treat an image URL as permission to redistribute its contents.
- Handle no result, multiple results, bad images, timeouts, rate limits, and offline state.
- Never advertise “scan any craft supply.”

No shared secret embedded in the APK.
No developer-funded backend assumed.
Do not send custom provider credentials to an untrusted or arbitrary endpoint.

If no approved provider is available, ship useful local scanning and manual entry. Document online lookup as deferred rather than presenting a fake feature.

